      "blockId": "tour:lead:e3456bc1f4d270f4",
      "field": "lead",
      "sourceTextSha256": "ec35ce9ae38c2234246b6f20b25838212a3381e56f3644d59bd77a366047e921",
      "text": "Brazil is a country of powdery white-sand beaches, verdant rainforests and rhythm-filled cities, with colonial towns, thundering waterfalls and tropical islands, and one of the richest collections of plant and animal species on Earth. In Rio de Janeiro, young football fans can see the legendary Maracanã, where Pelé once played, and young historians can discover the story of the Portuguese royal family; Sugar Loaf and Christ the Redeemer complete the experience. Next come the Iguazu Falls, explored from Brazil, and the Bird Park, full of fabulous birds; and finally a long family stay by the calm sea in Búzios.",
